                    {
                        "id":  "mass-combat-logistics",
                        "title":  "Logistical Support in Mass Combat",
                        "category":  "Warfare",
                        "summary":  "Food, reinforcements, healing, repairs, rest, and morale support determine whether an army can continue fighting.",
                        "body":  [
                                     "Logistics sustains forces beyond the immediate clash. Providing supplies prevents exhaustion and panic, reinforcements replace losses, medicine preserves troops, and repairs keep weapons, armor, vehicles, and airships operational.",
                                     "Rest and entertainment can restore effectiveness and morale. A force with tactical success but collapsing support may still be compelled to retreat or surrender."
                                 ],
                        "sections":  [
                                         {
                                             "heading":  "Legacy Logistics Procedures",
                                             "sectionType":  "mechanics-legacy",
                                             "body":  [
                                                          "The source assigns checks and example numerical effects for morale, unit health, reinforcements, casualty reduction, and duration. These procedures require conversion."
                                                      ]
                                         }
                                     ],
