                    {
                        "id":  "mass-combat-magical-assistance",
                        "title":  "Magical Assistance in Mass Combat",
                        "category":  "Warfare",
                        "summary":  "Battlefield magic can damage formations, preserve allies, alter capabilities, reshape terrain, or summon reinforcements.",
                        "body":  [
                                     "Spellcasters act as force multipliers when their magic is applied to units and battlefield conditions. Area attacks reduce concentrated forces, healing preserves formations, and enhancements or hindrances shift relative effectiveness.",
                                     "Control magic can change weather, terrain, visibility, and movement, while summoned allies create temporary forces capable of disruption or reinforcement."
                                 ],
                        "sections":  [
                                         {
                                             "heading":  "Legacy Magical Procedures",
                                             "sectionType":  "mechanics-legacy",
                                             "body":  [
                                                          "The source provides spellcasting rolls and example casualty, health, attack, and defense modifiers. These numerical procedures require conversion."
                                                      ]
                                         }
