                    {
                        "id":  "mass-combat-tracking",
                        "title":  "Mass Combat Tracking",
                        "category":  "Warfare",
                        "summary":  "Battle resolution follows force strength, morale, resources, weather, and terrain rather than casualties alone.",
                        "body":  [
                                     "Force strength records active troops and losses caused by fighting, magic, and sabotage. Morale reflects leadership, reversals, victories, and support, while resources determine how long each side can remain effective.",
                                     "Weather and terrain can block reinforcements, reduce visibility, create defensive positions, or magnify magical influence. These tracks together describe whether an army remains capable of pursuing its goals."
                                 ],
