                    {
                        "id":  "mass-combat-victory-conditions",
                        "title":  "Mass Combat Victory Conditions",
                        "category":  "Warfare",
                        "summary":  "Armies can win through destruction, seizure of key targets, morale collapse, or completion of scenario objectives.",
                        "body":  [
                                     "Total elimination is only one path to victory. Capturing commanders, ships, siege engines, or other critical assets may decide a battle before either force is destroyed.",
                                     "A side whose morale collapses may retreat or surrender. Battles can also be decided by specific objectives such as holding a location, completing a raid, protecting a convoy, or delaying an enemy advance."
                                 ],
